%% Sequence — merchant creates an order through the API (report sequence 2)
%% Based on seq-merchant-order.md by Sudari Ratnayake (Role 5); corrected against docs/architecture.md v1.2 §6.1, §6.2, §6.3, §10.2
%% Changes: /api/v1 prefix; gateway X-API-Key presence check and per-key rate limit; idempotent replay as alt/else;
%% event published by the outbox relay (not inline); X-Internal-Token on internal calls; webhook through webhook.q with retry.
%% Each service's own database, Redis and the outbox relay are shown as notes to keep the diagram readable.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Store as Merchant store server
    participant GW as api-gateway :8080
    participant MS as merchant-service :8085
    participant PS as parcel-service :8083
    participant PR as pricing-service :8082
    participant MQ as RabbitMQ
    participant NS as notification-service :8086

    Store->>GW: POST /api/v1/merchant-api/orders<br/>X-API-Key · body incl. idempotencyKey
    alt no X-API-Key header
        GW-->>Store: 401 ProblemDetail
    else over the per-key rate limit (Redis)
        GW-->>Store: 429 Too Many Requests
    end
    GW->>MS: forward with X-Request-Id
    MS->>MS: find key by SHA-256 hash in merchant_db
    alt unknown, revoked or expired key
        MS-->>Store: 401 ProblemDetail (via GW)
    else merchant not APPROVED
        MS-->>Store: 403 ProblemDetail (via GW)
    else @Valid fails
        MS-->>Store: 400 ProblemDetail (via GW)
    end
    MS->>MS: look up (merchant_id, idempotencyKey)
    alt order already exists (store retried)
        MS-->>Store: 200 existing order, nothing created
    else new order
        MS->>PS: POST /internal/parcels · X-Internal-Token
        PS->>PR: POST /internal/pricing/quote · X-Internal-Token
        alt weight does not fit size
            PR-->>PS: 400
            PS-->>MS: 400, nothing saved
            MS-->>Store: 400 ProblemDetail (via GW)
        else pricing down or slow (2 s / 5 s timeouts)
            PS-->>MS: 503
            MS-->>Store: 503 ProblemDetail (via GW)
        else quote OK
            PR-->>PS: 200 fee breakdown and total (LKR)
            Note over PS: one transaction in parcel_db:<br/>parcel CREATED + history row<br/>+ outbox event PENDING
            PS-->>MS: 201 {id, trackingNo, CREATED, feeAmount}
            MS->>MS: save merchant_orders row
            MS-->>Store: 201 Created {trackingNo, status, feeAmount} (via GW)
        end
    end

    Note over PS,NS: asynchronous, about 1 s later
    PS->>MQ: OutboxRelay publishes ParcelStatusChanged<br/>(parcel.status.created), marks row SENT after confirm
    MQ-)NS: webhook.q (merchantId is set)
    NS->>MS: GET /internal/merchants/{id}/webhook · X-Internal-Token
    MS-->>NS: {webhookUrl, secret}
    NS->>Store: POST webhook URL, signed:<br/>X-SwiftDrop-Signature: sha256=HMAC(body)
    alt 2xx
        Store-->>NS: 200, delivery recorded SUCCESS
    else non-2xx or timeout
        NS->>MQ: retry 10 s → 1 m → 5 m → parking
    end
